			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> to be honest, doing this opened a new perspective of how much overcomplicated stuff JS allows you to do without thinking, which is not a great thing... regular solutions are usually covered by TS, and in other cases you can always use an escape hatch of ts-expect-error or type casting...</p>",
