			"author": {
				"name": "Braw ☕🏳️‍🌈",
				"url": "https://mstdn.social/@brawaru",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/380/201/982/554/664/original/4cd79a5fec5ff5fb.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-07-26T19:31:43.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> is this VS Code? I noticed a completely different error in TypeScript playground, which I also spotted on the screenie: you forgot the generic type parameter for Array. Seems to work for me like this: <a href=\"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?filetype=js#code/MYGwhgzhAEAqCmEAu0DeBYAUASGAewDtkAnAV2CT2IAoBKNLbbJACwEsIA6YxeJOgNyMAvlkY8IfOgxzYA9ACoF0AAJIAngAd4aAILFiYdQB5U0AmAC28AFzQSbAgHNowgHzDoCuY2bsumiCkTo4wALzQANoAukI4ophY0MnQigpJKV6qmmCGlmgOzp4W1hkp3oxgACZVAApBIQTUJfD0GLI8SKTEBNCsHJyBwaGDpBAs1GYtrrRx2AkJWPAAHppUKGYIyK4CQA\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">typescriptlang.org/play/?filet</span><span class=\"invisible\">ype=js#code/MYGwhgzhAEAqCmEAu0DeBYAUASGAewDtkAnAV2CT2IAoBKNLbbJACwEsIA6YxeJOgNyMAvlkY8IfOgxzYA9ACoF0AAJIAngAd4aAILFiYdQB5U0AmAC28AFzQSbAgHNowgHzDoCuY2bsumiCkTo4wALzQANoAukI4ophY0MnQigpJKV6qmmCGlmgOzp4W1hkp3oxgACZVAApBIQTUJfD0GLI8SKTEBNCsHJyBwaGDpBAs1GYtrrRx2AkJWPAAHppUKGYIyK4CQA</span></a></p>",
